0..48 Comment "//! This source shows how strings share buffers."
49..52 Comment "//!"
53..131 Comment "//! A long string copy shares a buffer. A short string copy copies only inline"
132..187 Comment "//! bytes. A write leaves every other string unchanged."
188..191 Comment "//!"
192..270 Comment "//! The holder count controls each write. `push` copies a shared buffer before"
271..330 Comment "//! it writes. It writes a buffer with one holder in place."
331..334 Comment "//!"
335..362 Comment "//! - see: #1481 — `long`"
363..441 Comment "//! - cites: [Racordon-2022-implementation_strategies_mutable_value_semantics]"
442..445 Comment "//!"
446..630 Comment "//! [Racordon-2022-implementation_strategies_mutable_value_semantics]: https://doi.org/10.5381/jot.2022.21.2.a2 \"Racordon et al., Implementation strategies for mutable value semantics\""
